This module adopts the same governance shape as the rest of the Devotica
catalog (terraform-aws-vpc / iam / s3 / kms / rds / alb): unified Foundation
Plan §15.2 tagging, the central reusable CI workflow in
devotica-labs/terraform-shared-config, and conftest policies from
devotica-labs/terraform-policies.

It is the application-compute layer that ties the rest together:

  terraform-aws-vpc   → private subnet IDs the tasks run in
  terraform-aws-alb   → target group the service registers with + the ALB
                        security group allowed as ingress
  terraform-aws-kms   → key that encrypts the CloudWatch log group + secrets
  terraform-aws-iam   → (optional) externally-managed task / execution roles
  terraform-aws-rds   → the service's task role is granted DB access; the
                        DB security group allows ingress from this module's
                        service security group

Fintech-safe defaults: private networking (assign_public_ip = false),
ECS Exec off, Container Insights on, read-only container root filesystem,
KMS-encryptable logs, ARM64/Graviton runtime, 2 tasks for HA, and a service
security group that only admits the configured source SGs on the container
port.

v0.1 scope is a single-container Fargate service. Deferred: sidecar
containers, Cloud Map service discovery, EFS volumes, and blue/green
CodeDeploy — see the README scope table.

